  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Yes let me know when done and continue with next tasks". Issue #2814 (read it in full: gh issue view 2814) and DI-155 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. In `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Wizard/WizardShell.tsx` the reset-on-open effect dispatches `GO_TO_STEP` with `clearSkipped`; that case in `wizardShellReducer.ts` rebuilds only the config map and keeps the dynamic follow-on steps (for example "Create Event") in `state.steps`, so a wizard reopened in the same session shows last session's follow-on steps in its stepper. Finish is unaffected (selectedActions is cleared). Line numbers on origin/master 2ac250cae4 differ from the issue's; search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer: shared Fluent v9 React components (@spaarke/ui-components), WizardShell.</role>
  <goal>On reopen, the wizard's step list is back to its static steps; adding a follow-on step afterwards works as before; nothing else in WizardShell changes.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Fix it in the reducer's reset (or a dedicated reset action if GO_TO_STEP+clearSkipped is used elsewhere for a non-reset purpose: grep every dispatch first and keep those callers' behaviour). WizardShell is used by many wizards (CreateRecordWizard hosts, DecisionWizard, Work Assignment, create wizards with Send Email follow-ons): keep keyboard focus and step navigation tests green.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
